%% Fig. 5 - Sequence of a scan, from upload to results
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Analyst
  participant W as Web app
  participant A as Supabase Auth
  participant S as Storage (private)
  participant D as PostgreSQL (RLS, RPC)
  participant K as Worker
  participant G as Semgrep
  participant O as OpenAI

  U->>W: Sign in
  W->>A: email + password
  A-->>W: JWT session
  U->>W: Create project, choose ZIP and rule sets
  W->>D: insert project (RLS: owner = user)
  W->>S: upload ZIP to user-id/project-id/
  W->>D: create_scan_job() validates path and settings
  D-->>W: job queued
  loop every few seconds
    K->>D: claim_next_scan_job()
  end
  D-->>K: job (status running)
  K->>S: download archive
  K->>K: validate and extract safely, classify files
  loop for each batch of files
    K->>D: check cancel flag
    K->>G: scan batch with rule sets
    G-->>K: JSON results
    K->>D: progress (batches_done, heartbeat)
  end
  K->>K: normalise, deduplicate, redact
  K->>O: embed finding queries
  K->>D: match_knowledge_chunks() + CWE match
  K->>K: risk score and priority
  K->>D: worker_upsert_findings(), references, coverage
  W->>D: poll job status and findings
  D-->>W: results (only the user's projects)
  U->>W: Open finding, ask for explanation
  W->>K: /api/rag/ask (JWT)
  K->>A: verify JWT
  K->>O: embed question, then chat with excerpts
  O-->>K: answer citing excerpts
  K-->>W: grounded answer + sources
